+# Broadcom research consulted
+
+Accessed 2026-08-15.
+
+- **VCF Upgrade Failure: Cannot Upgrade VCF 5.2.2 to 9.0.1 or 9.0.2 Due to NSX Back-in-Time Error (NSX 4.2.3.3)** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/430825 — Accessed 2026-08-15 — Established that NSX 4.2.3.3 build 25171318 cannot move to the older NSX build in the VCF 9.0.2.0 bundle, and that VCF 9.1 is the supported forward route.
+- **Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630 — Accessed 2026-08-15 — Established the 5.2.x-to-9.1 management sequence: upgrade Operations first and use lifecycle workflows, with VCF Management Services and the centralized license service in the 9.1 architecture.
+- **vCenter Server Back-in-time release upgrade restriction** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/312157 — Accessed 2026-08-15 — Confirmed the general upgrade-path rule that a nominally higher major version is not supported when it would regress the release chronology and fixes.
